    "narrative": "The **Austin Waves** lineup for July 27th is anchored by **Gunnar Henderson** and **Luis Robert Jr.**, our strongest plays of the day. **Gunnar Henderson** (81.88) enjoys a prime matchup against K. Montero; his 6% boost from the #3 hole and dynamic platoon advantage make him an elite start. Similarly, **Luis Robert Jr.** (77.14) is poised for a high-ceiling performance against M. P\u00e9rez, bolstered by a 17% SP skill adjustment and a significant platoon edge. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) also warrants attention; despite the pedigree of the opposing starter, the 5.89 xERA and a 14% platoon boost make him a high-efficiency play as he hits in the favorable #2 spot.\n\nOur decision-making process was heavily influenced by the scarcity of stolen bases, which kept **Nasim Nunez** (62.15) in the starting lineup despite his #9 spot in the order. His score is propped up by a 4% increase due to the opposing pitcher\u2019s slow delivery, a key factor in our internal sprint-speed weighting. The toughest bench decision involved **Miguel Vargas** (51.80), who remained just outside the optimal start window. While his xwOBA of 0.390 is attractive, he lost out to the higher projected efficiency and better lineup positioning of **Jacob Wilson** (62.19) and **Curtis Mead** (53.86). We are closely monitoring weather reports for the **Heliot Ramos** (55.47) matchup against Sproat; while he remains a start, his score is tempered by a 2% penalty for the opposing pitcher's elite ability to hold runners, which slightly suppresses his stolen base upside.",
